From 649a34ec37c37636be7345bf6cddd7a60826f7ad Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Zhu, Jia-Xin" <j.zhu@fz-juelich.de>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 17:52:03 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] feat(lmp): add kspace style pppm/electrode/dplr

fix dplr puts part of the charge on massless Wannier centroids, so every
electrostatic solver has to hand the force on those sites back to fix dplr,
which pushes it onto the host atoms through the DipoleChargeModifier.
pppm/dplr does that by overriding fieldforce_ik()/fieldforce_ad() to stash the
k-space force in a private fele vector instead of adding it into atom->f;
FixDPLR::post_force picks it up via get_fele().

Constant-potential electrochemistry needs the same hand-off from the ELECTRODE
package's solver, which fix electrode/conp drives. Without it the k-space force
on the centroids lands on sites that carry no dynamics and is lost.

PPPMElectrodeDPLR is to pppm/electrode what PPPMDPLR is to pppm: the two
fieldforce_* overrides are the same text as pppm/dplr's, and compute() is a copy
of PPPMElectrode::compute() that drops the Ewald self-energy from the global
energy so elong keeps the convention the DPLR model was trained with. The
per-atom self term in eatom is left alone, again as in pppm/dplr.

Two deviations from a verbatim copy, both forced by access control:
PPPMElectrode::start_compute() is private, so compute() does inline what it does
minus the compute_step guard (which only skips a repeated particle_map(), and
repeating it is correct) and minus its first-call setup() (Verlet::setup() and
Min::setup() already call kspace->setup() before compute() is reached). The
compute_vector_called fast path and its reset go for the same reason -- that
flag is private too -- which leaves the density rebuilt from scratch every step,
exactly as upstream does unconditionally from LAMMPS 29 Aug 2024 on.

Unlike pppm/dplr and the earlier out-of-tree copies of this file, the
constructor does not set triclinic_support = 1: KSpace already defaults it to 1
and PPPMElectrode::init() rejects triclinic outright, so the assignment only
read as a support claim the base class contradicts.

ELECTRODE joins KSPACE and EXTRA-FIX as a build dependency, in builtin.cmake and
in the plugin CMakeLists (pppm_electrode.cpp plus the boundary-correction
sources it needs). Note ELECTRODE supports only the CMake build upstream, so the
Install.sh check makes the legacy make path unavailable on this branch;
patch/202404-fix_dplr-a0 remains the ELECTRODE-free reference patch.

Everything is guarded on LAMMPS_VERSION_NUMBER >= 20221222, where the Grid3d
communication API used by the copied compute() landed. Verified to compile
against the 2 Aug 2023, 29 Aug 2024 and 22 Jul 2025 stable releases (update4)
and against current LAMMPS master.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
